  "notes": "Straight, never swung, and the snare is a backbone instead of an engine: 2 and 4 with a clap and a stomp stacked a millisecond behind them, a tambourine running steady 8ths, toms and shakers as percussion candy, and the fill saved for the 8-bar turnaround. Major keys and open guitar shapes — I–V–vi–IV and its rotations under a sus2 Nashville wash — with a boom-chick bass alternating root and fifth rather than mirroring a kick. That is the whole distance from the train beat it extends: same kit, same key vocabulary, a snare lane an order of magnitude sparser. A real kit, so no 808.",
